## Employee Information
SCPL is committed to respecting the confidentiality of its employees’ personal Information as specified in this Code. It is Saptagir Camphor Private Limited’s policy to acquire and retain only personal data required for SCPL’s operation.
## Personal Data
Employees are responsible for providing HR with accurate personal data, and for notifying HR promptly with any updates.
## Guidelines
The following guidelines apply to all staff, at all levels, in using employee information:
- Employees with access to the personal data of other employees may not, under any circumstances, show, e‐mail, SMS or pass hard copies of this information to employees who are not authorized to have this information;
- Access to personal data is strictly limited to SCPL personnel with appropriate authorization and a clear business need for that information;
- Those with access to personal employees’ data may use it only for the purpose for which it was collected;
- Employee data may not be supplied to people or organizations outside SCPL unless they are authorized to have the information;
- Personal data must not be held longer than necessary to meet the legal or business reason for which authorization was given.
## Email & Electronic Records
It is SCPL Policy that Internet and e‐mail access, by all employees and third party consultants, from within SCPL’s network is used for business purposes. Although all employees using the service can enjoy private and confidential use of the system while performing their duties; they must note that all usage of the Internet and e‐mail is monitored and logged. Management reserves the right to review incoming and outgoing mail and web sites visited from within SCPL’s network. All SCPL employees and third party consultants must comply with the following rules and existing SCPL IT Policies:
- Internet and e‐mail access is to be used for business purposes;
- All SCPL Internet and e‐mail activity may be monitored and can be traced and consent to this monitoring is implied when users (employee or third party consultant) access the Internet and/ or SCPL e‐mail boxes, from within SCPL network;
- Unauthorized access or misuse of SCPL Internet and e‐mail is forbidden. Users must not use the Internet or e‐mail facility to access unauthorized, inappropriate or potentially offensive web sites, chat rooms etc., or to send non‐business related e‐mail;
- Any inappropriate, potentially offensive, obscene or derogatory information ore‐ mail messages received must be immediately deleted and must not be printed out or passed on or circulated to others, either by e‐ mail or hard copy;
- All physical Internet and external e‐mail connections from within SCPL network, must be routed through Saptagir Camphor Private Limited's firewalls on approval from the IT Department;
- Any other connections to the Internet from any equipment connected to SCPL network is strictly forbidden, this includes but is not limited to dial‐up access to all ISP via modem / ISDN / WAP;
- The sending of confidential information to external e‐mail addresses is not permitted. In exceptional cases, where the business requires SCPL confidential information to be sent to external e‐mail addresses over the Internet, prior approval must be obtained from the IT department;
- Employees and third party consultants are not permitted to automatically forward e‐mail messages addressed to Saptagir Camphor Private Limited e‐mail boxes to external e‐mail addresses;
- Employees and consultants are not authorized to retrieve, intercept or read any e‐mail messages that are not addressed to them;
- Each user will be assigned a network ID and password that they are responsible for and they must not disclose it to anyone else under any circumstances;
- Downloads of files from unknown or unauthorized sites are not allowed, as there is a risk of virus infection;
- Users are forbidden to download/install applications, software or plug‐ins themselves, from any source, on to any Computer within SCPL and in case of a business requirement, the software must be requested from the IT department;
- Users are forbidden to use any unlicensed or pirated software. In the event that they identify any software for which they have a business need, which is not currently provided, they must contact the IT Department. Users suspecting that the software on their computer is unlicensed or pirated should contact the IT Department immediately;
- Users are forbidden from connecting any personal computers / computer equipment (including smart‐phones and tablets) to SCPL network, as this introduces the risk of a virus infection.
## Document Retention
Certain types of documents and records must be retained for specific periods of time, because of legal and regulatory requirements or contractual obligations. If you are in doubt
- About which documents must be retained, for how long and in what form, consult your reporting manager, HR Department.
